Significant changes / 主要改动
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Rebranding: product name, identifiers, UI strings, logos, and assets
   changed from CyberStrikeAI to HostTraceAI.
2. Product scope narrowed: the platform now serves host provenance and
   incident response only, and explicitly excludes vulnerability scanning,
   penetration testing, asset discovery, alerting, and C2 functionality.
3. Built-in tool set reduced to reviewed, read-only or approval-gated host
   forensic tools (`binwalk`, `exiftool`, `foremost`, `strings`, `exec`).
   Non-forensic tooling was removed.
4. Investigation role set redesigned (`roles/`): trace commander, malware
   triage, and WebShell triage.
5. Host-forensics Skill library added and reorganised (`skills/`).
6. Governance defaults tightened: read-only collection by default, and file
   deletion, credential attempts, lateral movement, network scanning, and
   unreviewed script execution are disabled by default.

